<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shams al-Din Ali ibn Mas'ud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shams al-Din Ali ibn Mas'ud was the founder of the Mihrabanid dynasty of maliks in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistan">Sistan</a>, on the borders of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>. He established his rule in 1236, after the Mongol devastation ended the Nasrid maliks. His family claimed descent from the pre-Islamic Persian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saffarid-dynasty">Saffarids</a> and ruled Sistan under Mongol, Timurid and Safavid overlords for three centuries.</p></div>
